{"name":"Garden Club","hex":"#60784f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"},{"term":"club","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy object, often a kind of stick, intended for use as a bludgeoning weapon or a plaything.\n\n An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as golf.\n An item used during routines, the apparatus consisting of a set of two clubs.","An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as golf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with a club.","To score a victory over by a large margin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden club","blocks":[{"text":"A garden club is an organized group of people with a shared interest in gardening, gardens, and plants. A flower club is a similar group with a focus on flowers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Klamath_Blue_Star_Memorial_Highway.jpg/330px-Klamath_Blue_Star_Memorial_Highway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_club","wikidata":"Q5522367"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip